Human Atlas — interactive 3D anatomy viewer
===========================================

Anatomical model data
---------------------
This project embeds and redistributes derivative works (decimated and re-packed
meshes) of the BodyParts3D dataset:

  BodyParts3D, (c) The Database Center for Life Science
  licensed under CC Attribution-Share Alike 2.1 Japan
  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/lic.html

Files under public/atlas/ are derived from BodyParts3D 4.0 element meshes
(isa_BP3D_4.0_obj_99). They have been welded, decimated, re-scaled, quantised and
re-packed; no anatomy was added or invented. Structure names and identifiers come
from the Foundational Model of Anatomy (FMA) via the BodyParts3D mapping tables.

Because the source data is share-alike, this viewer as a whole is distributed under
CC Attribution-Share Alike 2.1 Japan.

Structure text and Portuguese names
-----------------------------------
Lead paragraphs shown in the detail panel are excerpts from Wikipedia (English and
Portuguese editions), licensed CC BY-SA. The article each excerpt came from is named
in the panel and linked from it. The mapping from FMA identifiers to those articles,
and the Portuguese names, come from Wikidata (property P1402), licensed CC0.

